# Line endings: the repository stores LF everywhere.
# The PowerShell engine is CRLF-agnostic, but its BOM is NOT optional — see below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The PowerShell scripts contain Chinese comments and string literals, and they
# must keep their UTF-8 BOM.
#
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 (the engine's target runtime) decodes a .ps1 file using
# the system ANSI code page unless the file starts with a BOM. Without it, the
# Chinese comments become mojibake and the parser can fail outright — the file
# literally will not run.
#
# `-text` disables all newline and encoding normalization for these paths so git
# never rewrites them. Do not change this to `text` or add a `working-tree-encoding`:
# either can strip the BOM and silently break the engine on a fresh clone.
*.ps1 -text
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Binary assets, if any are ever added.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
